concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-amendment-act-2018-sch-1-sec-46 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "46 Functions of Chief Executive"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-46 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Chief Executive has the responsibility of managing the affairs of the Authority.  (2) The Authority may give written directions to the Chief Executive about the management of the Authority’s affairs.  (3) The Chief Executive must comply with a direction under subsection (2).  (4) Subsection (3) does not apply to the extent that the direction relates to the Chief Executive’s performance of functions or exercise of powers under the Public Service Act 1999.  (5) A direction under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.  Governance arrangements  Schedule 1 Saving and transitional provisions  Part 2  No. 32, 2018 Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Amendment Act 2018" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Chief Executive has the responsibility of managing the affairs of the Authority.  (2) The Authority may give written directions to the Chief Executive about the management of the Authority’s affairs.  (3) The Chief Executive must comply with a direction under subsection (2).  (4) Subsection (3) does not apply to the extent that the direction relates to the Chief Executive’s performance of functions or exercise of powers under the Public Service Act 1999.  (5) A direction under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.  Governance arrangements  Schedule 1 Saving and transitional provisions  Part 2  No. 32, 2018 Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Amendment Act 2018"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "19924d8893e8c873c7e892899a56122c97430be1ff0d0db60f0ac3aa863ddab1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
